lake|inland-water|NOUN|large inland area of water|A large area of water surrounded by land.|hồ|The footpath circles the lake before reaching the old mill.|Đường đi bộ vòng quanh hồ trước khi tới cối xay cũ.|Countable; by or beside a lake for the shore, in a lake for the water. Lake is capitalized in many proper names.|0
risky|involving-risk|ADJECTIVE|involving possible harm or loss|Involving a chance of harm, loss, or another unwanted result.|rủi ro; mạo hiểm; nguy hiểm|Relying on a single supplier proved risky when deliveries stopped.|Việc phụ thuộc vào một nhà cung cấp duy nhất tỏ ra rủi ro khi các đợt giao hàng ngừng lại.|Riskier and riskiest change y to i; risky to do something evaluates a proposed action without guaranteeing a bad result.|0
surrounding|nearby-on-all-sides|ADJECTIVE|nearby and around a place|Around or near a particular place on its different sides.|xung quanh; lân cận|The market serves the town and the surrounding villages.|Khu chợ phục vụ thị trấn và các làng xung quanh.|Normally before a noun, as in surrounding area or surrounding buildings. It identifies a place relative to a central location.|0
wealth|riches|NOUN|large amount of valuable possessions|A large amount of money or valuable possessions.|sự giàu có; của cải|The family's wealth came from a trading business established decades earlier.|Sự giàu có của gia đình đến từ một doanh nghiệp buôn bán được thành lập nhiều thập kỷ trước.|Uncountable; personal wealth or accumulate wealth. A wealthy person has wealth, but a single valuable item is not a wealth.|0
wealth|abundance|NOUN|large supply of something useful|A large supply or variety of something useful or valuable.|sự phong phú; nguồn dồi dào|The archive offers a wealth of information about local crafts.|Kho tư liệu cung cấp thông tin phong phú về các nghề thủ công địa phương.|Normally a wealth of something; the following noun may be uncountable or plural. This figurative pattern differs from financial riches.|1
determined|firm-in-intention|ADJECTIVE|firm in an intention|Firmly intending to do something and unwilling to give up easily.|quyết tâm; kiên quyết|The young drummer was determined to master the difficult rhythm.|Người chơi trống trẻ quyết tâm làm chủ nhịp điệu khó.|Determined to do something; a determined effort names purposeful persistence. This differs from the passive verb form in a date was determined.|0
